IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 4: POWERS AND APPOINTMENTS, ss 27 to 37.
-- These sections address officials and bodies. They are encoded for what they decide; the seat layer
-- keeps only what they mean to a person (who may act, and whether an act is valid).
-- Policy for "unless the contrary intention appears": a plain yes/no input, NOTHING when it is TRUE.

§ `Section 27 -- construction of provisions as to exercise of powers and duties`

-- src:1313 | 27.—(1) Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty,
-- src:1314 | then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be
-- src:1315 | exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as
-- src:1316 | occasion requires.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1313-1316)
GIVEN `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires` `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers a power or imposes a duty` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Who may exercise the power of an office` IS ONE OF
    `the holder of the office for the time being`
    `a person duly appointed to act for the holder`
    `someone else`

-- src:1318 | (2) Where a written law confers a power or imposes a duty on the
-- src:1319 | holder of an office as such, then, unless the contrary intention
-- src:1320 | appears, the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed
-- src:1321 | by the holder of the office for the time being or by a person duly
-- src:1322 | appointed to act for him or her.
@ref s 27(2) (src:1318-1322)
GIVEN `the power or duty is conferred on the holder of an office as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person` IS A `Who may exercise the power of an office`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` `the power or duty is conferred on the holder of an office as such` `the person` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the power or duty is conferred on the holder of an office as such` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the person`
         WHEN `the holder of the office for the time being` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person duly appointed to act for the holder` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What a power to make subsidiary legislation, issue an order or do an act includes` IS ONE OF
    `the power to amend`
    `the power to vary`
    `the power to rescind`
    `the power to revoke`
    `the power to suspend`
    `the power to abstain from doing the act`
    `something else`

-- src:1324 | (3) Where any Act confers a power to make subsidiary legislation,
-- src:1325 | to issue any order or to do any act, the power is, unless the contrary
-- src:1326 | intention appears, to be construed as including the power exercisable
-- src:1327 | in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions (if any)
-- src:1328 | to amend, vary, rescind, revoke or suspend the subsidiary legislation
-- src:1329 | made or order issued or any part thereof or to abstain from doing the
-- src:1330 | act.
@ref s 27(3) (src:1324-1330)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power to make subsidiary legislation, to issue an order or to do an act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is asked about` IS A `What a power to make subsidiary legislation, issue an order or do an act includes`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` `an Act confers a power to make subsidiary legislation, to issue an order or to do an act` `what is asked about` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `an Act confers a power to make subsidiary legislation, to issue an order or to do an act` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `what is asked about`
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 28 -- power to appoint includes power to dismiss`

DECLARE `What a power to appoint includes` IS ONE OF
    `the power to dismiss a person appointed`
    `the power to suspend a person appointed`
    `the power to appoint another person temporarily in place of a person suspended`
    `the power to appoint another person temporarily in place of a sick or absent holder`
    `something else`

-- src:1334 | 28.—(1) Where a written law confers upon any person or authority
-- src:1335 | a power to make appointments to any office or place, the power is,
-- src:1336 | unless the contrary intention appears, to be construed as including a
-- src:1337 | power to dismiss or suspend any person appointed and to appoint
-- src:1338 | another person temporarily in the place of any person so suspended or
-- src:1339 | in place of any sick or absent holder of the office or place.
@ref s 28(1) (src:1334-1339)
GIVEN `a written law confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is asked about` IS A `What a power to appoint includes`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to appoint includes this` `a written law confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place` `what is asked about` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `what is asked about`
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1341 | (2) Where the power of the person or authority to make
-- src:1342 | appointments is only exercisable upon the recommendation or
-- src:1347 | subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority,
-- src:1348 | the power of dismissal is, unless the contrary intention appears, only
-- src:1349 | exercisable upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or
-- src:1350 | consent of that other person or authority.
@ref s 28(2) (src:1341-1350)
GIVEN `the power to appoint is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dismissal is on that recommendation or subject to that approval or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power of dismissal is exercisable` `the power to appoint is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of another` `the dismissal is on that recommendation or subject to that approval or consent` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the power to appoint is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of another` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST `the dismissal is on that recommendation or subject to that approval or consent`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 29 -- construction of enabling words`

-- src:1354 | 29.—(1) Where a written law confers powers on any person to do or
-- src:1355 | enforce the doing of any act or thing, such powers are to be
-- src:1356 | understood to be also conferred as are reasonably necessary to enable
-- src:1357 | the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing.
@ref s 29(1) (src:1354-1357)
GIVEN `a written law confers powers on a person to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power is understood to be also conferred` `a written law confers powers on a person to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing` `the power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers powers on a person to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing`
    THEN JUST `the power is reasonably necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it`
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `A power s 29(2) speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `a power to prohibit, control or regulate a matter`
    `a power to grant a licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption`
    `some other power`

DECLARE `What s 29(2) says it includes` IS ONE OF
    `power to provide for the matter by licensing it`
    `power to prohibit acts whereby the prohibitions, control or regulations might be evaded`
    `power to impose reasonable conditions subject to which the licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption may be granted`
    `something else`

-- src:1359 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1) —
-- src:1361 | (a) a power to prohibit or to control or to regulate any matter
-- src:1362 | includes power to provide for the same by the licensing
-- src:1363 | thereof and power to prohibit acts whereby the
-- src:1364 | prohibitions, control or regulations affecting the matter
-- src:1365 | might be evaded;
-- src:1367 | (b) a power to grant a licence, permit, authority, approval or
-- src:1368 | exemption includes power to impose reasonable conditions
-- src:1369 | subject to which the licence, permit, authority, approval or
-- src:1370 | exemption may be granted.
@ref s 29(2) (src:1359-1370)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `A power s 29(2) speaks of`
      `what it includes` IS A `What s 29(2) says it includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `the power` `what it includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `a power to prohibit, control or regulate a matter` THEN
        CONSIDER `what it includes`
        WHEN `power to provide for the matter by licensing it` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `power to prohibit acts whereby the prohibitions, control or regulations might be evaded` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a power to grant a licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption` THEN
        CONSIDER `what it includes`
        WHEN `power to impose reasonable conditions subject to which the licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption may be granted` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `some other power` THEN NOTHING

§ `Sections 30 to 32 -- appointments`

DECLARE `How an appointment is made` IS ONE OF
    `by naming a person`
    `by directing the person for the time being holding a designated office`
    `some other way`

-- src:1374 | 30.—(1) Where by or under any Act, the President, a Minister or
-- src:1375 | any public officer or body is empowered to appoint or name a person
-- src:1376 | to have and exercise any powers or perform any duties, the President,
-- src:1377 | Minister, public officer or body may either appoint a person by name
-- src:1378 | or direct the person for the time being holding the office designated
-- src:1379 | by the President, Minister, public officer or body to have and exercise
-- src:1380 | those powers and perform those duties.
-- src:1382 | (2) Thereupon, or from the date specified by the President,
-- src:1383 | Minister, public officer or body, the person appointed by name or
-- src:1384 | the person holding the office as mentioned in subsection (1) has and
-- src:1385 | may exercise those powers or perform those duties accordingly.
@ref s 30(1), (2) (src:1374-1385)
GIVEN `the President, a Minister or any public officer or body is empowered by or under an Act to appoint or name a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how` IS A `How an appointment is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointment is made in a way section 30 allows` `the President, a Minister or any public officer or body is empowered by or under an Act to appoint or name a person` `how` MEANS
    IF `the President, a Minister or any public officer or body is empowered by or under an Act to appoint or name a person`
    THEN CONSIDER `how`
         WHEN `by naming a person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `by directing the person for the time being holding a designated office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `some other way` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1387 | (3) Any such appointment may be made with retrospective effect to
-- src:1388 | any date not being a date earlier than the commencement of the Act
-- src:1389 | under which the appointment is made.
@ref s 30(3) (src:1387-1389)
GIVEN `the date the appointment is to take effect` IS A DATE
      `the commencement of the Act under which the appointment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment may be made with retrospective effect to that date` `the date the appointment is to take effect` `the commencement of the Act under which the appointment is made` MEANS
    `the date the appointment is to take effect` AT LEAST `the commencement of the Act under which the appointment is made`

-- src:1396 | 31. When reference is made in any written law, instrument, warrant
-- src:1397 | or process of any kind made or issued by the President, a Minister,
-- src:1398 | any public officer or body or person having authority under any
-- src:1399 | written law to make or to issue the same to any public officer by the
-- src:1400 | term designating his or her office, such public officer includes the
-- src:1401 | officer for the time being executing the duties of that office or any
-- src:1402 | portion of those duties.
@ref s 31 (src:1396-1402)
GIVEN `a reference to a public officer is by the term designating his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is for the time being executing the duties of that office or a portion of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the public officer referred to includes this officer` `a reference to a public officer is by the term designating his or her office` `the officer is for the time being executing the duties of that office or a portion of them` MEANS
    `a reference to a public officer is by the term designating his or her office`
    AND `the officer is for the time being executing the duties of that office or a portion of them`

-- src:1406 | 32. Any appointment may be declared to have effect as from the
-- src:1407 | date upon which the appointee commenced to exercise the powers
-- src:1408 | and discharge the duties of his or her appointment, not being a date
-- src:1409 | earlier than the date of the commencement of the written law under
-- src:1410 | which the appointment is made.
@ref s 32 (src:1406-1410)
GIVEN `the day the appointee commenced to exercise the powers and discharge the duties` IS A DATE
      `the commencement of the written law under which the appointment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day from which the appointment may be declared to have effect` `the day the appointee commenced to exercise the powers and discharge the duties` `the commencement of the written law under which the appointment is made` MEANS
    IF `the day the appointee commenced to exercise the powers and discharge the duties` AT LEAST `the commencement of the written law under which the appointment is made`
    THEN JUST `the day the appointee commenced to exercise the powers and discharge the duties`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 32A -- power of majority, quorum, etc., of board, etc.`

-- src:1446 | (5) In this section, “statutory body” means a board, commission,
-- src:1447 | committee or similar body, whether corporate or unincorporate,
-- src:1448 | established under a written law.
@ref s 32A(5) (src:1446-1448)
GIVEN `it is a board, commission, committee or similar body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a statutory body for section 32A` `it is a board, commission, committee or similar body` `it is established under a written law` MEANS
    `it is a board, commission, committee or similar body` AND `it is established under a written law`

-- src:1414 | 32A.—(1) Where a written law confers a power or function or
-- src:1415 | imposes a duty upon a statutory body consisting of 3 or more persons,
-- src:1416 | the power may be exercised, or the function or duty may be
-- src:1417 | performed, by a majority of those persons.
-- src:1443 | (4) This section is subject to any provision to the contrary in any
-- src:1444 | written law.
@ref s 32A(1), (4) (src:1414-1444)
GIVEN `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who agree` IS A NUMBER
      `a written law provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` `the number of those persons who agree` `a written law provides to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `a written law provides to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST ((`the number of those persons who agree` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `the number of persons the statutory body consists of`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1419 | (2) Where a statutory body consists of 3 or more persons —
-- src:1421 | (a) a quorum is constituted at a meeting of the body by a
-- src:1422 | number of members of the body equal to —
-- src:1424 | (i) if the written law establishing the body fixes the
-- src:1425 | number of members of the body — at least half of
-- src:1426 | that number of members; and
-- src:1428 | (ii) if the number of persons is not so fixed but is within a
-- src:1429 | range having a maximum or minimum — at least
-- src:1430 | half of the number of members in office; and
@ref s 32A(2)(a) (src:1419-1430)
GIVEN `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` IS A NUMBER
      `the written law establishing the body fixes the number of members at` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `a written law provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a quorum is constituted at the meeting` `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` `the written law establishing the body fixes the number of members at` `the number of members in office` `the number of members present at the meeting` `a written law provides to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `a written law provides to the contrary`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the written law establishing the body fixes the number of members at`
         WHEN JUST fixed THEN JUST ((`the number of members present at the meeting` TIMES 2) AT LEAST fixed)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST ((`the number of members present at the meeting` TIMES 2) AT LEAST `the number of members in office`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1419 | (2) Where a statutory body consists of 3 or more persons —
-- src:1432 | (b) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the
-- src:1433 | body present at the meeting, if those members constitute a
-- src:1434 | quorum, is to be regarded as having been done by the body.
@ref s 32A(2)(b) (src:1419-1434)
GIVEN `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` IS A NUMBER
      `those present constitute a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those present who agree` IS A NUMBER
      `a written law provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` `those present constitute a quorum` `the number of members present` `the number of those present who agree` `a written law provides to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons the statutory body consists of` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `a written law provides to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST (`those present constitute a quorum` AND ((`the number of those present who agree` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `the number of members present`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1439 | (3) At a meeting of a statutory body, the chairperson or other
-- src:1440 | member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote in all
-- src:1441 | matters in which a decision is taken by vote.
@ref s 32A(3) (src:1439-1441)
GIVEN `it is a meeting of a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a decision is taken by vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the chairperson or other member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote` `it is a meeting of a statutory body` `a decision is taken by vote` `a written law provides to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `it is a meeting of a statutory body` AND `a decision is taken by vote` AND (NOT `a written law provides to the contrary`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 33 and 33A -- boards`

DECLARE `A circumstance s 33 mentions` IS ONE OF
    `a vacancy in the membership`
    `a defect later discovered in the appointment or qualification of a person purporting to be a member`
    `a minor irregularity in convening a meeting`
    `something else`

-- src:1452 | 33. Where by or under any Act, any board, commission, committee
-- src:1453 | or similar body, whether corporate or unincorporate, is established,
-- src:1454 | then, unless the contrary intention appears, the powers of such board,
-- src:1455 | commission, committee or similar body are not affected by —
-- src:1457 | (a) any vacancy in the membership thereof;
-- src:1459 | (b) the fact that it is afterwards discovered that there was some
-- src:1460 | defect in the appointment or qualification of a person
-- src:1461 | purporting to be a member thereof; or
-- src:1463 | (c) the fact that there was any minor irregularity in the
-- src:1464 | convening of any meeting thereof.
@ref s 33 (src:1452-1464)
GIVEN `a board, commission, committee or similar body is established by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance` IS A `A circumstance s 33 mentions`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the powers of the body are affected` `a board, commission, committee or similar body is established by or under an Act` `the circumstance` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a board, commission, committee or similar body is established by or under an Act` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the circumstance`
         WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1468 | 33A. Where any written law confers on a statutory body the power
-- src:1469 | to invest any moneys in accordance with the standard investment
-- src:1470 | power of statutory bodies, then, subject to any general or special
-- src:1471 | directions as the Minister charged with responsibility for that
-- src:1472 | statutory body may issue, that statutory body may —
-- src:1474 | (a) invest those moneys in the manner it thinks fit; and
-- src:1476 | (b) engage in any financial activity or participate in any
-- src:1477 | financial arrangement for the purpose of managing or
-- src:1478 | hedging against any financial risk that arises or is likely to
-- src:1479 | arise from such investment.
@ref s 33A (src:1468-1479)
GIVEN `a written law confers on a statutory body the power to invest moneys in accordance with the standard investment power of statutory bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has issued directions that bind the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the body may invest the moneys in the manner it thinks fit, and engage in financial activity or arrangements to manage or hedge risk from the investment` `a written law confers on a statutory body the power to invest moneys in accordance with the standard investment power of statutory bodies` `the Minister has issued directions that bind the body` MEANS
    IF `a written law confers on a statutory body the power to invest moneys in accordance with the standard investment power of statutory bodies`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the Minister has issued directions that bind the body`) -- "subject to any general or special directions": the directions displace the default
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 34, 35, 35A, 37 -- how an exercise of power is signified or a document signed`

DECLARE `Under whose hand` IS ONE OF
    `any Minister`
    `the Secretary to the Cabinet`
    `the President himself or herself`
    `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible`
    `a public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister`
    `the chairperson of the statutory body`
    `a member of the statutory body duly authorised by it to do so in place of the chairperson`
    `someone else`

-- src:1488 | 34.—(1) Where any power is conferred upon the President to make
-- src:1489 | any subsidiary legislation or appointment, give any direction, issue
-- src:1490 | any order, authorise any thing or matter to be done, grant any
-- src:1491 | exemption, remit any fee or penalty or exercise any other power
-- src:1492 | under any written law, it is sufficient if the exercise of such power by
-- src:1493 | the President is signified under the hand of any Minister or the
-- src:1494 | Secretary to the Cabinet.
-- src:1496 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the power of the President to
-- src:1497 | make or issue any warrants or proclamations which may be made or
-- src:1498 | issued only under the hand of the President himself or herself.
@ref s 34 (src:1488-1498)
GIVEN `the exercise of a power by the President is signified under the hand of` IS A `Under whose hand`
      `the power is to make or issue a warrant or proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `the exercise of a power by the President is signified under the hand of` `the power is to make or issue a warrant or proclamation` MEANS
    IF `the power is to make or issue a warrant or proclamation`
    THEN JUST (`the exercise of a power by the President is signified under the hand of` EQUALS `the President himself or herself`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exercise of a power by the President is signified under the hand of`
         WHEN `any Minister` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the Secretary to the Cabinet` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1502 | 35. Where any written law confers upon a Minister power to make
-- src:1503 | any subsidiary legislation or appointment, give any direction, issue
-- src:1504 | any order, authorise any thing or matter to be done, grant any
-- src:1505 | exemption, remit any fee or penalty or exercise any other power, it is
-- src:1506 | sufficient, unless in the written law it is otherwise provided, if the
-- src:1507 | exercise of such power by the Minister is signified under the hand of
-- src:1508 | the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is
-- src:1509 | responsible or of any public officer duly authorised in writing by the
-- src:1510 | Minister.
@ref s 35 (src:1502-1510)
GIVEN `the exercise of a power by the Minister is signified under the hand of` IS A `Under whose hand`
      `the written law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the exercise of the Minister's power is sufficiently signified` `the exercise of a power by the Minister is signified under the hand of` `the written law otherwise provides` MEANS
    IF `the written law otherwise provides` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exercise of a power by the Minister is signified under the hand of`
         WHEN `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1514 | 35A.—(1) Where a statutory body is permitted by any written law
-- src:1515 | to delegate the performance of any of the statutory body’s functions
-- src:1516 | or the exercise of any of the statutory body’s powers, that power to
-- src:1517 | delegate does not extend to the power to make any subsidiary
-- src:1518 | legislation.
@ref s 35A(1) (src:1514-1518)
GIVEN `a statutory body is permitted by a written law to delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to delegate extends to making subsidiary legislation` `a statutory body is permitted by a written law to delegate` MEANS
    IF `a statutory body is permitted by a written law to delegate` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1522 | (2) Where any Act confers upon a statutory body power to make
-- src:1523 | subsidiary legislation, it is sufficient, unless in such Act it is
-- src:1524 | otherwise provided, if the exercise of that power by the statutory body
-- src:1525 | is signified under the hand of —
-- src:1527 | (a) the chairperson of the statutory body; or
-- src:1532 | (b) a member of the statutory body duly authorised by that
-- src:1533 | body to do so in place of the chairperson.
@ref s 35A(2) (src:1522-1533)
GIVEN `the exercise of a power by the statutory body is signified under the hand of` IS A `Under whose hand`
      `an Act otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the exercise of the statutory body's power to make subsidiary legislation is sufficiently signified` `the exercise of a power by the statutory body is signified under the hand of` `an Act otherwise provides` MEANS
    IF `an Act otherwise provides` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exercise of a power by the statutory body is signified under the hand of`
         WHEN `the chairperson of the statutory body` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a member of the statutory body duly authorised by it to do so in place of the chairperson` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1611 | 37. Where in any written law any document is required to be under
-- src:1612 | the hand of or countersigned by a Minister in exercise of any powers
-- src:1613 | conferred thereby, it is sufficient for the document to be under the
-- src:1614 | hand of or signed or countersigned by the Permanent Secretary to the
-- src:1615 | Ministry for which the Minister is responsible or by any public officer
-- src:1616 | duly authorised in writing by the Minister.
@ref s 37 (src:1611-1616)
GIVEN `the document is signed or countersigned by` IS A `Under whose hand`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the requirement that a document be under the hand of or countersigned by a Minister is met` `the document is signed or countersigned by` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document is signed or countersigned by`
    WHEN `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 36 -- delegation of functions of Minister`

DECLARE `Who a Minister's function is delegated to` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the responsible Minister`
    `a public body or a public officer`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `What is delegated` IS ONE OF
    `a function`
    `a power to make subsidiary legislation`
    `the power of delegation in section 36`

-- src:1539 | 36.—(1) Where an Act confers or imposes a function on a Minister
-- src:1540 | (called in this section the responsible Minister), the Minister may
-- src:1541 | delegate the function in accordance with this section.
-- src:1543 | (2) Unless any Act expressly provides otherwise, the function may,
-- src:1544 | with the Prime Minister’s approval, be delegated to any Minister,
-- src:1545 | Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime
-- src:1546 | Minister to assist the responsible Minister.
-- src:1548 | (3) Unless the contrary intention appears in any Act, the function
-- src:1549 | may be delegated to a public body or a public officer.
-- src:1578 | (6) This section does not permit the delegation of —
-- src:1580 | (a) any power to make subsidiary legislation; and
-- src:1585 | (b) the power of delegation in this section.
-- src:1587 | (7) A function delegated under this section may not be further
-- src:1588 | delegated by the delegate.
@ref s 36(1) to (3), (6), (7) (src:1539-1588)
GIVEN `an Act confers or imposes the function on a Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is delegated` IS A `What is delegated`
      `to whom` IS A `Who a Minister's function is delegated to`
      `the Prime Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is further delegating` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation is permitted by section 36` `an Act confers or imposes the function on a Minister` `what is delegated` `to whom` `the Prime Minister approves` `the Act expressly provides otherwise` `a contrary intention appears in an Act` `the delegate is further delegating` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an Act confers or imposes the function on a Minister` THEN NOTHING
        IF `what is delegated` EQUALS `a power to make subsidiary legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `what is delegated` EQUALS `the power of delegation in section 36` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the delegate is further delegating` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `to whom`
            WHEN `a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the responsible Minister` THEN
                IF `the Act expressly provides otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the Prime Minister approves`
            WHEN `a public body or a public officer` THEN
                IF `a contrary intention appears in an Act` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE
            WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1551 | (4) Where a function is delegated under this section —
-- src:1553 | (a) the delegate may or must (as the case may be) exercise the
-- src:1554 | function; and
-- src:1556 | (b) if the Act that created the function provides that the
-- src:1557 | exercise of the function depends on the Minister’s opinion,
-- src:1558 | belief or state of mind, the delegate may exercise the
-- src:1559 | function based on the delegate’s opinion, belief or state of
-- src:1560 | mind.
@ref s 36(4) (src:1551-1560)
GIVEN `a function is delegated under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act that created the function makes its exercise depend on the Minister's opinion, belief or state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegate may exercise the function based on the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` `a function is delegated under section 36` `the Act that created the function makes its exercise depend on the Minister's opinion, belief or state of mind` MEANS
    IF `a function is delegated under section 36` AND `the Act that created the function makes its exercise depend on the Minister's opinion, belief or state of mind`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `A feature of a delegation` IS ONE OF
    `made by order in the Gazette`
    `general or limited`
    `subject to conditions consistent with the nature of the delegated function`
    `to a named person or to the holder of an office`
    `to 2 or more persons at the same time`
    `preventing the responsible Minister from personally exercising the delegated function`
    `something else`

-- src:1562 | (5) A delegation under this section —
-- src:1564 | (a) must be made by order in the Gazette;
-- src:1566 | (b) may be general or limited;
-- src:1568 | (c) may be subject to conditions that are consistent with the
-- src:1569 | nature of the delegated function;
-- src:1571 | (d) may be to a named person or to the holder of an office;
-- src:1573 | (e) may be to 2 or more persons at the same time; and
-- src:1575 | (f) does not prevent the responsible Minister from personally
-- src:1576 | exercising the delegated function.
@ref s 36(5) (src:1562-1576)
GIVEN `the feature` IS A `A feature of a delegation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 36(5) says a delegation` `the feature` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the feature`
    WHEN `made by order in the Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE -- "must be made": a requirement
    WHEN `general or limited` THEN JUST TRUE -- "may be"
    WHEN `subject to conditions consistent with the nature of the delegated function` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `to a named person or to the holder of an office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `to 2 or more persons at the same time` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `preventing the responsible Minister from personally exercising the delegated function` THEN JUST FALSE -- "does not prevent"
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1562 | (5) A delegation under this section —
-- src:1564 | (a) must be made by order in the Gazette;
@ref s 36(5)(a) a delegation must be made by order in the Gazette (src:1562-1564)
GIVEN `the delegation is made by order in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation meets the requirement of form in section 36(5)(a)` `the delegation is made by order in the Gazette` MEANS
    `the delegation is made by order in the Gazette`

-- src:1590 | (8) This section does not affect the operation of any rule of law by
-- src:1591 | which any function conferred or imposed on a Minister may be
-- src:1592 | exercised by another person on behalf of the Minister.
@ref s 36(8) (src:1590-1592)
GIVEN `a rule of law allows another person to exercise the function on behalf of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36 affects the operation of that rule of law` `a rule of law allows another person to exercise the function on behalf of the Minister` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:1594 | (9) In this section —
-- src:1596 | (a) “function” includes power and duty, and the exercise of a
-- src:1597 | function includes the performance of a duty;
-- src:1599 | (b) “public body” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:1600 | Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 (Act 5 of 2018), and
-- src:1601 | “public officer” includes a person deemed to be a public
-- src:1602 | officer by section 21(1) of that Act; and
-- src:1604 | (c) a reference to an Act does not include any subsidiary
-- src:1605 | legislation made under the Act.
-- src:1607 | [Act 4 of 2021 wef 01/03/2024]
@ref s 36(9) (src:1594-1607)
GIVEN `the reference is to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in section 36 a reference to an Act includes subsidiary legislation made under the Act` `the reference is to an Act` MEANS
    FALSE
